<title>UK: HORSE RACING-ROYAL ASCOT RESULTS.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-ROYAL ASCOT RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>ASCOT, England 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of feature races</p>
<p>on the first day of the four-day Royal Ascot meetng on Tuesday:</p>
<p>Queen Anne Stakes, a group two race for three-year-olds and</p>
<p>upwards, run over one mile (1.6 kms)</p>
<p>1. Allied Forces  10-1 (ridden by Frankie Dettori)</p>
<p>2. Centre Stalls  11-1 (Richard Quinn)</p>
<p>3. Ali-Royal	 9-4 favourite (Kieren Fallon)</p>
<p>11 ran.</p>
<p>Distances: A neck, one and a quarter lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by the Godolphin group and by Saaed Bin Suroor</p>
<p>at Newmarket in England.</p>
<p>Value to winner: 65,000 pounds sterling ($106,000)</p>
<p>Prince of Wales Stakes, a group two race for three-year-olds</p>
<p>and upwards, run over two miles (3.2 kms)</p>
<p> 1. Bosra Sham    11-4 ON favourite (Kieren Fallon)</p>
<p> 2. Alhaarth	10-1 (Frankie Dettori)</p>
<p> 3. London News   10-1 (D.J.Whyte)</p>
<p>Seven ran.</p>
<p>Distances: Eight lengths, five lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by W.Said and trained by Henry Cecil at</p>
<p>Newmarket in England.</p>
<p>Value to winner: 67,310 pounds sterling ($109,715)</p>
<p>St James's Palace Stakes, a group one race for</p>
<p>three-year-old colts and fillies, run over one mile (1.6 kms)</p>
<p>1. Starborough 11-2 (Frankie Dettori)</p>
<p>2. Air Express 20-1 (Brett Doyle)</p>
<p>3. Daylami	7-2 (Gerald Mosse)</p>
<p>Eight ran. Desert King was the 2-1 favourite.</p>
<p>Distances: One length, four lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Sheikh Mohammed and trained by David Loder</p>
<p>in England.</p>
<p>Value to winner: 134,680 pounds sterling ($219,530)</p>
</text>
